summary_comment:
Stratigraphic trap within multi-phase fill channel complex with very small four-way dip closure. Seismic facies/mounding are indicative of sandstone presence, with the stratigraphic nature of the trap (including lateral seal) more difficult to map without the bright amplitudes on the Ultra-Far Coloured Inversion volume, which are indicative of hydrocarbons.

Amplitude brightsare cut and offset by small faults suggesting a bottom seal within a multi-phase fill within the channel. 

CI amplitudes are greater than those seen at the Elke Main Discovery and the presence of gas is possible, though this could also be indicative of less biodegraded oil.&#039;
